  "description": "The execution-backend port of Fuaran.Modelling — the manager's entire backend-facing surface as one interface (submit fits, read outcomes, resolve a vintage, score, query artifacts, request a re-vintage), every operation returning a typed refusal in the error channel. Its types are FSharp.Core-only records mirroring a language-neutral model-execution wire specification field for field, with a canonical codec (declaration-ordered records, sorted maps, sign-prefixed 64-bit integers, ECMAScript real numbers), the submitter-side minting canonicalisation, a drift-conformance harness that fails the build when the specification moves, and a deterministic in-memory reference executor that is explicitly not statistics.",
